    title: "Bangalore to Coorg Road Trip: Complete 3-Day Itinerary by Tempo Traveller",
    slug: "bangalore-to-coorg-road-trip-itinerary-tempo-traveller",
    excerpt: "The definitive guide to planning a 3-day road trip from Bangalore to Coorg with family or groups — highway routes via Hassan vs Mysore, scenic stops, coffee estate stays, and why a Tempo Traveller is the ideal vehicle.",
    coverImageKey: "/assets/images/destinations/coorg-getaway.webp",
    content: `<p>Coorg (Kodagu) sits nestled in the Western Ghats around 250 to 270 km from Bangalore, depending on whether you take the classic Mysore Expressway route or the scenic Hassan highway (NH75). Known for rolling coffee and spice estates, misty valleys, and welcoming homestays, it is consistently Bangalore's favourite weekend escape. When travelling as a family or friend group of 8 to 16 people, renting a private chauffeured <a href="/fleet/tempo-traveller" class="text-brand-700 underline font-medium">Tempo Traveller</a> transforms the journey from exhausting convoy driving into an enjoyable, unified road trip.</p>

<h2>Choosing the Best Route from Bangalore to Coorg</h2>
<p>There are two primary driving corridors connecting Bangalore to Madikeri (the heart of Coorg):</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Route 1 (via Mysore Expressway &amp; Kushalnagar - 250 km, ~5.5 hours):</strong> Bangalore &rarr; Mandya &rarr; Mysore Ring Road &rarr; Hunsur &rarr; Kushalnagar &rarr; Madikeri. This is the smoothest route with fast highway speeds on the expressway, though weekend toll queues and Kushalnagar traffic can add time.</li>
  <li><strong>Route 2 (via NH75 Hassan &amp; Channarayapatna - 275 km, ~6 hours):</strong> Bangalore &rarr; Nelamangala &rarr; Kunigal &rarr; Channarayapatna &rarr; Holenarasipura &rarr; Arakalgud &rarr; Madikeri. This route bypasses Mysore entirely, offers tranquil rural scenery, and allows an easy detour to the historic Hoysala temples of Belur and Halebidu.</li>
</ul>

<h2>The Ideal 3-Day Itinerary for Groups</h2>
<h3>Day 1: Arrival, Golden Temple &amp; Raja's Seat Sunset</h3>
<p>Depart Bangalore early by 6:00 AM to beat the Goraguntepalya / Kengeri morning exit congestion. Break for breakfast near Channapatna or Kunigal for authentic Karnataka Thatte Idli. By noon, reach Bylakuppe near Kushalnagar to visit the renowned <em>Namdroling Monastery (Golden Temple)</em>. After exploring the Tibetan settlement, head up to your plantation homestay near Madikeri. Wind down the evening watching the golden sunset from <em>Raja's Seat</em>.</p>

<h3>Day 2: Waterfalls, Dubare Elephants &amp; Coffee Plantation Walks</h3>
<p>Start Day 2 visiting <em>Dubare Elephant Camp</em> along the banks of the Cauvery River (morning bathing sessions run from 9:00 AM to 11:00 AM). Head towards <em>Abbey Falls</em>, walking through dense cardamom and coffee plantations. In the afternoon, arrange a guided coffee walking tour where estate owners explain the harvest of Arabica and Robusta berries. Spend the evening around a homestay campfire with authentic Kodava dishes like Pandi Curry and Kadambuttu.</p>

<h3>Day 3: Talakaveri Origin &amp; Scenic Drive Back</h3>
<p>On your final morning, visit <em>Talakaveri</em> (the holy birthplace of the River Cauvery atop the Brahmagiri hills) and the temple at Bhagamandala. After lunch, embark on your relaxed return journey to Bangalore, arriving comfortably by late evening.</p>

<h2>Why a Tempo Traveller Outperforms Multiple Small Cars</h2>
<p>Taking three separate cars for 12 people means paying three sets of tolls, coordinating three drivers on twisting hill roads, and losing the shared laughter of travelling together. With our <strong>12-seater or 17-seater Tempo Travellers</strong>, you get individual push-back seats, high-roof walking space, panoramic windows for scenic ghat views, and a dedicated boot for luggage. Most importantly, our experienced commercial chauffeurs are familiar with every ghat hairpin bend between Hunsur and Madikeri.</p>

<p>Ready to plan your trip? Check our ready-made <a href="/tour-packages/coorg-getaway" class="text-brand-700 underline font-medium">Coorg Getaway Package</a> or <a href="/contact" class="text-brand-700 underline font-medium">enquire directly</a> for transparent, per-km vehicle hire.</p>`,
