    title: "Bangalore to Chikmagalur Weekend Road Trip: Mullayanagiri, Coffee Estates & Temple Trail",
    slug: "bangalore-to-chikmagalur-weekend-road-trip-guide",
    excerpt: "Plan the ultimate weekend road trip from Bangalore to Chikmagalur — NH75 drive via Hassan, visiting Belur and Halebidu temples, climbing Mullayanagiri peak, and choosing the right vehicle for hill trails.",
    coverImageKey: "/assets/images/destinations/chikmagalur-coffee-trails.webp",
    content: `<p>Perched high in the Baba Budan Giri range of the Western Ghats, Chikmagalur is the historic cradle where coffee was first cultivated in India by the Sufi saint Baba Budan in 1670. Located approximately 245 km west of Bangalore, it offers the perfect 2 to 3 day road trip for travellers looking for crisp mountain air, cascading waterfalls, and world-class Hoysala temple architecture.</p>

<h2>The Highway Route: Bangalore to Chikmagalur (245 km, ~4.5 to 5 hours)</h2>
<p>The journey along <strong>NH75</strong> is one of the best-maintained national highways in Karnataka:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Bangalore &rarr; Nelamangala Toll &rarr; Kunigal &rarr; Channarayapatna &rarr; Hassan Bypass &rarr; Belur &rarr; Chikmagalur.</li>
  <li>Four-lane access-controlled driving allows smooth cruising all the way to Hassan (180 km in ~3 hours). The final 65 km from Hassan through Belur to Chikmagalur passes through lush paddy fields, ancient banyan avenues, and the foothills of the Western Ghats.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Key Attractions to Include in Your Itinerary</h2>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Mullayanagiri Peak:</strong> At 1,930 metres (6,330 ft), this is the highest summit in Karnataka. A well-paved road winds up to the base steps, from where a short 500-step trek leads to the Shiva temple at the crown, offering panoramic 360-degree views across sea-like cloud formations.</li>
  <li><strong>Baba Budangiri &amp; Manikyadhara Falls:</strong> Renowned for sacred shrines, unique mountain formations, and perennial waterfalls surrounded by herbal shola grasslands.</li>
  <li><strong>Belur &amp; Halebidu UNESCO Heritage Sites:</strong> Built in the 12th century by Hoysala monarchs, the Chennakeshava Temple at Belur and Hoysaleshwara Temple at Halebidu feature intricate chloritic schist stone carvings of dancing celestial maidens (Madanikas) and mythological epics.</li>
  <li><strong>Coffee Plantation Homestays:</strong> Wake up to bird calls and fresh filter coffee on private estates in Mudigere, Aldur, and Mallandur.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Choosing the Best Vehicle for Chikmagalur's Hill Roads</h2>
<p>While the highway to Hassan is broad and modern, the inner roads to Mullayanagiri, Bababudangiri, and secluded homestays have narrow shoulders, steep hairpins, and occasional monsoon ruts. For small families, the <a href="/fleet/car/innova-crysta" class="text-brand-700 underline font-medium">Toyota Innova Crysta</a> or <a href="/fleet/car/maruti-ertiga" class="text-brand-700 underline font-medium">Maruti Ertiga</a> provides high ground clearance and excellent torque. For larger corporate offsites or multi-family holidays, our <a href="/fleet/tempo-traveller" class="text-brand-700 underline font-medium">12-seater or 17-seater Tempo Travellers</a> navigate these hills with ease under the guidance of our verified commercial chauffeurs.</p>

<p>Plan your weekend getaway with our <a href="/tour-packages/chikmagalur-coffee-trails" class="text-brand-700 underline font-medium">Chikmagalur Tour Package</a> or <a href="/contact" class="text-brand-700 underline font-medium">request a tailored quotation</a> today.</p>`,
